import ../../../ui/source_language.dl

set first to a UI source document named "first.dl" at "file:///workspace/first.dl" prefixed by "" containing "first means: 1" using UI CPU analysis
set second to a UI source document named "second.dl" at "file:///workspace/second.dl" prefixed by "" containing "second means: 2" using UI CPU analysis
set client to a UI language client rooted at "file:///workspace"
set client's project to first's project
set client's model to the UI language model for first in client
set client's document to first
set client's uri to first's uri
set client's context to first's context
set client's project context to first's project's context
set client's project revision to first's project's revision
set client's profiles to the compact JSON form of (first's project's profiles)
set work to the UI language opening in client
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC array
set work to the UI language reply response at step 4 in client
free response
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 6, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 6 in client
free response
require condition ((first needs UI source analysis) = false) reporting "The first source did not finish analysis."
free first's diagnostics
set first's diagnostics to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "message" is "Retained warning", JSON number "severity" is 2, JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line 0 and character 0 to line 0 and character 5)]]
set first's diagnostic revision to first's revision

set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing second at 0.0 seconds
require condition (work's step = 9) reporting "Switching projects did not close the first source."
free work's payload
# DynLex publishes this workspace refresh after processing didClose. It still
# needs a protocol reply, but the closed source has no tokens to refresh.
set response to a JSON array containing [
    a JSON object containing [JSON text "method" is "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", JSON child "params" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (first's uri), JSON child "diagnostics" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])],
    a JSON object containing [JSON text "jsonrpc" is "2.0", JSON number "id" is 99, JSON text "method" is "workspace/semanticTokens/refresh", JSON child "params" is (a new JSON-RPC object)]
]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 9 in client
free response
require condition ((first needs UI source analysis) = false) reporting "A refresh after didClose requeued the closed source and caused endless project switching."
require condition (first's diagnostics' length = 1) reporting "Closing a source discarded its retained diagnostics even though its cached analysis stayed current."
require condition (work's step = 13) reporting "A refresh from didClose was not acknowledged."
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC array
set work to the UI language reply response at step 13 in client
free response
require condition ((work's step = 10) and (client's document = second)) reporting "Replying to a closing refresh lost the next project."
free work's payload

free UI language client client
free UI source project (first's project)
free UI source project (second's project)
print line "Closing refreshes receive replies without requeuing closed source projects."
